  "id": "interitem-correlation",
  "term": "interitem correlation",
  "definition": "Interitem correlation is the degree to which the different items in a measure relate to one another. The average interitem correlation summarizes how strongly the items tend to move together across the scale and can be used when considering internal consistency or how independent the items are from each other.",
